/S /P
/ActualText (14)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
1143 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (2. Multi-line comments \(docstrings\): While Python doesn't have a specific syntax for multi-line comments, docstrings serve a similar purpose.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1144 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Docstrings are enclosed in triple quotes \(''' '''\) and are typically used to describe functions, modules, or classes.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
